WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.789 --> 00:00:03.462
[Chattering]
[Bell Tolling]

2
00:00:03.537 --> 00:00:06.484
[Man]
I didn't sleep well last night,
and I woke up with a scratchy throat.

3
00:00:06.552 --> 00:00:11.339
- I just don't feel so good. Uh, cough.
- ~ [Rock, Faint]

4
00:00:11.411 --> 00:00:17.100
[Clears Throat] Yeah, um-um,
I have a bit of an upset stomach too,
and I think I'm running a fever.

5
00:00:17.174 --> 00:00:22.189
I'm just worried
I might be contagious. [Coughs]

6
00:00:22.267 --> 00:00:27.122
Inventory. Tomorrow.
I'm-Yeah, I'm sure
I'll be feeling better by then.

7
00:00:28.131 --> 00:00:30.472
Thanks, Mr. Innabe.

8
00:00:32.252 --> 00:00:36.261
[Exhales, Chuckles]
I cannot believe you just did that.

9
00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:39.184
L-I really do have a cough.

10
00:00:39.255 --> 00:00:41.596
Oh. So you weren't lying.

11
00:00:41.667 --> 00:00:46.350
You'd be curled up in bed
with a bowl of chicken soup-
[Moans, Kisses]

12
00:00:46.425 --> 00:00:48.595
Even if you didn't have
a horny girl in your bed?

13
00:00:48.671 --> 00:00:52.680
Yes. [Laughs]
Because I really do- Hey.

14
00:00:52.759 --> 00:00:57.442
I really do have a cough.
You also have a little rash.

15
00:00:57.517 --> 00:01:03.206
[Laughs]
Um, I'm not sure
we should be kissing.

16
00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:07.461
Oh. [Kisses] It's okay.
Because I have almost
no interest in kissing you.

17
00:01:07.535 --> 00:01:10.036
Perfect.
[Laughs]
Good.

18
00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:15.264
Uh-uh-uh.
[Exhales, Laughs]

19
00:01:17.722 --> 00:01:20.635
Oh, baby.
[Exhales]

20
00:01:20.703 --> 00:01:22.645
[Both Moaning]

21
00:01:28.042 --> 00:01:30.783
[Moaning Continues]

22
00:01:37.926 --> 00:01:40.599
[Panting]

23
00:01:46.001 --> 00:01:50.284
[Breathing Erratically]

24
00:01:50.357 --> 00:01:55.817
[Giggles]
Oh, Brandon.

25
00:01:55.886 --> 00:01:59.895
[Chuckles]
Brandon.

26
00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:04.456
[Laughs]
I know I'm good,
but come on.

27
00:02:06.943 --> 00:02:09.078
Brandon?

28
00:02:10.964 --> 00:02:14.071
Brandon. Brandon. Brandon.

29
00:02:14.147 --> 00:02:17.323
Brandon.! Brandon.!

30
00:02:50.503 --> 00:02:55.499
[Woman On P.A.]
Any additional R.N. To Surgical.
Any additional R.N. To Surgical.

31
00:02:58.914 --> 00:03:03.079
[Labored Breathing]

32
00:03:07.026 --> 00:03:10.258
[Groans, Shudders]

33
00:03:10.332 --> 00:03:12.425
[House]
Why do you want me to treat this guy?

34
00:03:12.502 --> 00:03:14.493
Blood pressure's not responding
to I.V. Fluids.

35
00:03:14.570 --> 00:03:17.165
No, no. I didn't ask how you plan to
con me into treating him.

36
00:03:17.242 --> 00:03:19.905
I asked you why
you want me to treat him.

37
00:03:19.979 --> 00:03:22.642
He's sick. I care.
I'm pathetic.

38
00:03:22.716 --> 00:03:25.379
There are about a billion sick people
on the planet. Why this one?

39
00:03:25.453 --> 00:03:29.447
Because this one's
in our emergency room.
Ah, so it's a proximity issue.

40
00:03:29.526 --> 00:03:32.519
If somebody was sick in
the third-floor stairwell,
that's who'd we be talking about.

41
00:03:32.597 --> 00:03:35.761
Yes. I checked the stairwell.
It's clear.

42
00:03:35.835 --> 00:03:38.327
Okay, then.
Emergency room guy it is.
[Elevator Bell Dings]

43
00:03:38.405 --> 00:03:42.069
Wait. Why was that so easy?
You know why.

44
00:03:43.346 --> 00:03:46.748
- Blood pressure's not responding to
I.V. Fluids?
- Yeah.

45
00:03:48.220 --> 00:03:50.985
That's just weird.

46
00:03:52.726 --> 00:03:55.855
C.B.C. Was unremarkable.
Abdominal C.T. Scan didn't show anything.

47
00:03:55.931 --> 00:03:58.594
So, people, differential diagnosis.
What's wrong with her?

48
00:03:58.669 --> 00:04:00.603
- Him.
- Him. Her. Does it matter?

49
00:04:00.672 --> 00:04:04.837
Does anyone think
it's a testicular problem? No. So, Chase?

50
00:04:04.911 --> 00:04:07.904
- Yersinia infection?
- No. You wouldn't get the rash or cough.

51
00:04:07.982 --> 00:04:11.316
What about arthritis?
Accompanying vasculitis
causes nerve damage-

52
00:04:11.386 --> 00:04:15.187
- No. It wouldn't cause
the blood pressure problems. Allergy?
- The kid's got abdominal pain.

53
00:04:15.259 --> 00:04:17.524
Maybe carcinoid?
No. But then you wouldn't get the-

54
00:04:17.596 --> 00:04:22.194
Foreman, if you're going to list
all the things it's not,
it might be quicker to do it alphabetically.

55
00:04:22.269 --> 00:04:27.402
Let's see, now. "Absidia." Excellent.
Doesn't account for any of the symptoms.

56
00:04:27.477 --> 00:04:30.311
- No condition accounts for
all these symptoms.
- Oh, good.

57
00:04:30.381 --> 00:04:33.442
Because I thought maybe he was sick.
But, apparently, he's not.

58
00:04:33.520 --> 00:04:36.081
Who wants to do up
the discharge papers?
[Sighs]

59
00:04:37.224 --> 00:04:41.059
[Sighs] Okay. Unless we control
the blood pressure,

60
00:04:41.130 --> 00:04:44.294
he's gonna start circling the drain
before we can figure out
what's wrong with him.

61
00:04:44.369 --> 00:04:48.899
Treat him for sepsis, broad-spectrum
antibiotics, and I want a Cort-stim test
and an echocardiogram.

62
00:04:48.975 --> 00:04:51.809
[Heartbeat]
[Coughing]

63
00:04:55.385 --> 00:04:58.719
You all right?
[Coughs]
Yeah.

64
00:04:58.789 --> 00:05:02.954
The Cort-stim test will tell us
if your pituitary and adrenal glands
are working properly.

65
00:05:03.029 --> 00:05:06.193
- His glands? What does that mean?
- We have a few theories we're working on.

66
00:05:06.267 --> 00:05:08.930
- You mean you don't know.
- Mindy.

67
00:05:09.004 --> 00:05:11.769
I'm just saying, if they knew
they wouldn't be testing you,
they'd be treating you.

68
00:05:11.841 --> 00:05:16.803
Yeah, well, that's the way it works.
First we find out what it is,
then we get you better.

69
00:05:25.561 --> 00:05:28.622
You're half an hour late.
Busy caseload.

70
00:05:28.700 --> 00:05:31.067
One case is not a load.

71
00:05:31.136 --> 00:05:34.971
So how are we doing
on cotton swabs today? If there's
an acute shortage, I could run home-

72
00:05:35.042 --> 00:05:38.535
No, you couldn't.
Nice.

73
00:05:43.555 --> 00:05:46.923
Hello, sick people
and their loved ones.

74
00:05:46.993 --> 00:05:51.328
In the interest of saving time
and avoiding a lot ofboring
chitchat later, I'm Dr. Gregory House.

75
00:05:51.399 --> 00:05:55.666
You can call me Greg.
I'm one of three doctors
staffing this clinic this morning.

76
00:05:55.739 --> 00:05:59.870
Short. Sweet. Grab a file.
This ray of sunshine
is Dr. Lisa Cuddy.

77
00:05:59.945 --> 00:06:03.438
Dr. Cuddy runs this whole hospital,
so, unfortunately, she's much
too busy to deal with you.

78
00:06:03.517 --> 00:06:07.113
I am a board-certified diagnostician,

79
00:06:07.188 --> 00:06:09.783
with a double specialty of
infectious disease and nephrology.

80
00:06:09.860 --> 00:06:13.695
I'm also the only doctor
currently employed at this clinic who is
forced to be here against his will.

81
00:06:13.765 --> 00:06:16.257
That is true, isn't it? But not to worry.

82
00:06:16.336 --> 00:06:20.034
Because for most of you, this job could be
done by a monkey with a bottle of Motrin.

83
00:06:20.107 --> 00:06:24.204
Speaking of which,
if you're particularly annoying,
you may see me reach for this.

84
00:06:24.280 --> 00:06:27.944
This is Vicodin. It's mine.
You can't have any.

85
00:06:28.019 --> 00:06:32.013
And, no, I do not have
a pain management problem.
I have a pain problem.

86
00:06:32.092 --> 00:06:36.393
But who knows? Maybe I'm wrong.
Maybe I'm too stoned to tell.

87
00:06:36.465 --> 00:06:38.798
So, who wants me?

88
00:06:42.607 --> 00:06:45.076
And who would rather wait
for one of the other two guys?

89
00:06:46.813 --> 00:06:51.309
Okay. Well, I'll be in Exam Room One
if you change your mind.

90
00:06:53.590 --> 00:06:56.458
Jodi Matthews?

91
00:06:56.527 --> 00:06:59.827
Please accompany Dr. House
to Exam Room One.

92
00:07:04.740 --> 00:07:07.403
Dr. Chase.

93
00:07:07.477 --> 00:07:10.970
I'm not sure scaring your boyfriend
is the best medicine for him right now.

94
00:07:11.049 --> 00:07:15.384
I know. I get stupid
when I'm scared.
Don't go rock climbing.

95
00:07:15.455 --> 00:07:18.789
Look, I was wondering.
Before this happened, we were having sex.

96
00:07:21.196 --> 00:07:25.190
[Sighs]
What? You're wondering if
whatever he has, you might've gotten it?

97
00:07:25.269 --> 00:07:28.262
It-It's unlikely.
We ran a complete S.T.D. Panel, so-

98
00:07:28.340 --> 00:07:33.006
No. I'm wondering if maybe
I did this to him. I was kind of rough.

99
00:07:39.857 --> 00:07:43.692
It was yellow.
It was?

100
00:07:43.763 --> 00:07:46.892
It's not anymore.
Well, that's a shame.

101
00:07:46.967 --> 00:07:51.633
I thought that might be a problem,
so I brought you this.

102
00:07:55.146 --> 00:07:59.140
Your mucus was "pale goldenrod."

103
00:07:59.219 --> 00:08:02.917
Last week, yes.
Should I be worried?
Oh, yes. Very.

104
00:08:02.990 --> 00:08:06.427
Really?
I thought it was okay now.

105
00:08:06.496 --> 00:08:08.988
And yet, here you are.
What happened?

106
00:08:09.066 --> 00:08:11.627
Paramedics took a week
to respond to your 911 call?

107
00:08:11.703 --> 00:08:14.605
You're not a very nice doctor,
are you?

108
00:08:14.675 --> 00:08:17.406
And you are very bad at
whatever it is you do.

109
00:08:17.478 --> 00:08:20.778
You don't even know me.
I know you're gonna get fired.

110
00:08:20.850 --> 00:08:24.947
That's why you got the new glasses.
That's why your teeth are sparkly white.

111
00:08:25.022 --> 00:08:28.515
You're getting the most of
your health insurance while you still can.

112
00:08:30.030 --> 00:08:32.021
I might be quitting.
[Zipper Zips]

113
00:08:32.100 --> 00:08:36.596
If you were quitting, you'd have known
that last week when your snot was still
pale goldenrod. You're getting fired.

114
00:08:38.275 --> 00:08:40.938
I just don't like being told what to do.

115
00:08:44.951 --> 00:08:47.580
I can get you in
for a full body scan later this week.

116
00:08:47.656 --> 00:08:50.148
Thanks.

117
00:08:52.830 --> 00:08:55.664
It's got to be viral.
We should start running gels and titers.

118
00:08:55.734 --> 00:08:59.831
Maybe we should look into
the girlfriend's theory.
She thinks she rode him to death.

119
00:08:59.907 --> 00:09:03.275
[Chuckles]
What'd you tell her?

120
00:09:03.345 --> 00:09:05.814
I told her 22-year-old men
don't die of sex.

121
00:09:05.882 --> 00:09:07.975
- What'd you ask her?
- What do you mean?

122
00:09:08.052 --> 00:09:11.045
I mean, I hope you got some specifics
on exactly what was going on.

123
00:09:11.123 --> 00:09:14.958
If the girl thinks it could kill you,
it's worth knowing about.

124
00:09:18.467 --> 00:09:20.492
Have you ever taken a life?

125
00:09:30.084 --> 00:09:32.018
We should stop the antibiotics.

126
00:09:32.087 --> 00:09:34.021
It's too soon to say
they're not having an effect.

127
00:09:34.090 --> 00:09:36.183
They're having an effect.

128
00:09:37.729 --> 00:09:41.359
His B.P. 's falling fast.
There's fluid filling his lungs.

129
00:09:41.434 --> 00:09:43.699
His creatinine is rising.

130
00:09:49.713 --> 00:09:51.704
His kidneys are shutting down.

131
00:09:53.218 --> 00:09:57.417
Our treatment isn't making him better.
It's killing him.

132
00:10:00.662 --> 00:10:05.829
So, we had six symptoms that didn't
add up to anything. Now we got seven.
Who's excited?

133
00:10:05.902 --> 00:10:09.566
I don't think it complicates things.
The kidney failure was caused by
the antibiotics.

134
00:10:09.641 --> 00:10:14.307
- Maybe.
- Typically, low blood pressure
and abdominal pain means an infection.

135
00:10:14.382 --> 00:10:17.284
An abdominal infection causes sepsis,
low blood pressure.

136
00:10:17.353 --> 00:10:20.289
Except we checked for
abdominal infections.

137
00:10:20.357 --> 00:10:24.351
But what if it's the other way around?
What if the low blood pressure's
causing the abdominal pain?

138
00:10:24.430 --> 00:10:28.926
Viral heart infection.
The intestines aren't getting
enough blood, and the result is belly pain.

139
00:10:29.003 --> 00:10:32.963
- I know it's not
the standard presentation.
- It's a 10 million-to-1 shot.

140
00:10:33.043 --> 00:10:35.706
I thought that's what we dealt with here.

141
00:10:35.780 --> 00:10:41.448
It explains the cardiomyopathy, the pain,
the low B.P., the fever.

142
00:10:43.458 --> 00:10:47.623
You read the book.
Impressive.

143
00:10:47.697 --> 00:10:53.194
It's a ludicrously long shot that
explains every one of those symptoms-
except for the cough and the rash.

144
00:10:53.272 --> 00:10:56.936
Should we just erase those?
Well, anything can cause a rash.

145
00:10:58.680 --> 00:11:02.048
Okay. Cardiac infection.

146
00:11:03.554 --> 00:11:06.490
- Cameron, you thought allergy.
- Mm-hmm.

147
00:11:08.260 --> 00:11:10.957
Chase, what was it you thought?
Carcinoid?

148
00:11:11.031 --> 00:11:13.796
Then there's hypothyroidism.

149
00:11:13.869 --> 00:11:17.670
Could be parasites.

150
00:11:20.579 --> 00:11:22.513
Finally, sinus infection.

151
00:11:22.582 --> 00:11:26.212
If you're gonna list
all the things it can't be,
you're gonna need more colors.

152
00:11:26.286 --> 00:11:30.621
Cameron was right.
No condition explains all these symptoms.

153
00:11:31.795 --> 00:11:36.928
- But orange and green covers everything.
- Orange and green?

154
00:11:37.002 --> 00:11:40.029
Two conditions contracted simultaneously?

155
00:11:40.107 --> 00:11:43.373
Occam's Razor.
The simplest explanation
is always the best.

156
00:11:43.445 --> 00:11:46.415
- And you think one is simpler than two?
- Pretty sure it is, yeah.

157
00:11:48.418 --> 00:11:53.414
Baby shows up. Chase tells you that
two people exchanged fluids
to create this being.

158
00:11:53.493 --> 00:11:58.091
I tell you that one stork
dropped the little tyke off in a diaper.
Are you gonna go with the two or the one?

159
00:11:58.167 --> 00:12:00.796
- I think your argument is specious.
- I think your tie is ugly.

160
00:12:00.870 --> 00:12:05.935
Why is one simpler than two?
It's lower, lonelier. Is it simpler?

161
00:12:06.011 --> 00:12:09.106
Each one of these conditions
is about a thousand-to-one shot.

162
00:12:09.183 --> 00:12:12.847
That means that any two of them
happening at the same time
is a million-to-one shot.

163
00:12:12.922 --> 00:12:15.756
Chase says the cardiac infection
is a 10 million-to-1 shot,

164
00:12:15.825 --> 00:12:18.420
which makes my idea
10 times better than yours.

165
00:12:18.496 --> 00:12:21.295
Get a calculator. Run the numbers.

166
00:12:21.366 --> 00:12:22.890
We'll run the tests.
Tests take time.

167
00:12:22.969 --> 00:12:26.804
Treatment's quicker.
Start the kid on Unasyn
for the sinus infection,

168
00:12:26.875 --> 00:12:31.507
and... what was orange?
[Cameron]
Hypothyroidism.

169
00:12:31.582 --> 00:12:35.747
My uncle has hypothyroidism.
Not like this.

170
00:12:35.821 --> 00:12:39.451
Intravenous Levothyroxin
is an artificial thyroid medication
that should take care of it.

171
00:12:39.527 --> 00:12:43.020
Also, the nurses are going to
start you on Unasyn.
It's a more targeted antibiotic.

172
00:12:43.098 --> 00:12:44.759
For the sinus infection?
Yes.

173
00:12:44.834 --> 00:12:48.498
- The other stuff is
for something else entirely.
- Bad luck, huh?

174
00:12:48.573 --> 00:12:52.305
Don't worry. He should be
back to ditching work in no time.

175
00:12:52.379 --> 00:12:54.780
Brandon?

176
00:12:57.620 --> 00:13:01.955
Hey, Mom.
[Coughs]

177
00:13:02.026 --> 00:13:03.789
We're his parents.
How's he doing?

178
00:13:03.862 --> 00:13:06.354
Um, Brandon is-

179
00:13:06.432 --> 00:13:11.064
Uh, Mom. Dad-[Clears Throat]
This is Mindy.

180
00:13:12.241 --> 00:13:17.374
I was gonna bring her home for Christmas.
Um, we're engaged.

181
00:13:26.762 --> 00:13:30.927
[Woman On P.A.]
Dr. Hall to the recovery room.
Dr. Hall-

182
00:13:31.001 --> 00:13:32.662
Did you tell the family House's theory?

183
00:13:32.737 --> 00:13:36.731
Two odd conditions striking
completely coincidentally
at the exact same time?

184
00:13:36.810 --> 00:13:39.803
I didn't phrase it
quite that way.
They agree to treatment?

185
00:13:39.881 --> 00:13:43.215
Of course they did. We're doctors.
They believe whatever we tell them.

186
00:13:43.286 --> 00:13:45.949
So, is that our job?
House's puppets?

187
00:13:46.023 --> 00:13:48.857
He comes up with an insane idea,
we get to pretend it's not?

188
00:13:48.927 --> 00:13:52.091
His insane ideas are usually right.
We've been here long enough to-

189
00:13:52.166 --> 00:13:54.327
We've been here long enough
to have Stockholm syndrome.
[Laughs]

190
00:13:54.402 --> 00:13:59.068
What, because we don't hate him?
He thinks outside the box.
Is that so evil?

191
00:13:59.142 --> 00:14:01.805
He has no idea where the box is.

192
00:14:01.879 --> 00:14:06.545
If you guys think he's right, go home.
Relax. Just wait for
the kid to get all better.

193
00:14:06.619 --> 00:14:09.453
I'm going to the lab
to test for viral infections.

194
00:14:13.464 --> 00:14:15.398
[Groans]

195
00:14:20.173 --> 00:14:22.972
Negative for Coxsackie "B" virus.

196
00:14:23.044 --> 00:14:25.707
Seven down, about 5,000 to go.

197
00:14:25.781 --> 00:14:30.082
You really think we're gonna
come up with your mystery virus just by
running gels till we guess it right?

198
00:14:32.057 --> 00:14:35.653
No. I think we're gonna do it
by standing around
watching other people work.

199
00:14:35.729 --> 00:14:39.496
I'm waiting for
the Epstein-Barr virus.

200
00:14:43.073 --> 00:14:45.304
- She's weird, isn't she?
- Bad idea.

201
00:14:45.376 --> 00:14:48.710
- What?
- Bad idea. You work with her.

202
00:14:48.782 --> 00:14:50.716
What did I say?

203
00:14:50.785 --> 00:14:56.453
Is weird some new
ghetto euphemism for sexy,
like bad is good and phat is good?

204
00:14:56.526 --> 00:14:59.052
- Then what the hell does "good" mean?
- "Ghetto euphemism"?

205
00:14:59.129 --> 00:15:02.361
- [Scoffs]
- You don't think she's hot?

206
00:15:02.435 --> 00:15:04.232
No.

207
00:15:04.304 --> 00:15:08.766
Wow. Then you're brilliant.
And I am using "brilliant" as a euphemism.

208
00:15:08.844 --> 00:15:12.178
Obviously, the girl is hot.
Y-You're not talking about her aesthetics.

209
00:15:12.248 --> 00:15:14.683
You're talking about
if I want to jump her. I don't.

210
00:15:14.753 --> 00:15:16.812
Brilliant.

211
00:15:20.761 --> 00:15:23.663
- [Machine Beeps]
- Your Epstein-Barr is ready.

212
00:15:29.307 --> 00:15:31.640
What are you doing?
Level four.

213
00:15:31.710 --> 00:15:35.272
No, no. I mean-
I know what you meant.
We're waiting.

214
00:15:35.349 --> 00:15:38.717
My throat hurts.
So you said.

215
00:15:38.788 --> 00:15:43.284
How long are we waiting?
Two minutes less than when
you asked me two minutes ago.

216
00:15:45.197 --> 00:15:51.035
- Hi.
- Hi. I'm Dr. Cuddy.
Nice to meet you.

217
00:15:51.105 --> 00:15:55.771
Dr. Cuddy, thanks for the consult.
His throat seems to have some condition.

218
00:15:58.650 --> 00:16:01.916
Say "Ah."
Ah. [Mumbles]

219
00:16:03.423 --> 00:16:05.050
He has a sore throat.

220
00:16:06.895 --> 00:16:10.059
Of course. Yes, why didn't l-

221
00:16:10.133 --> 00:16:14.070
I mean, because he said that
it hurt, and I should have deduced
that meant it was sore.

222
00:16:14.139 --> 00:16:16.631
I was in a board meeting.
Patients come first, right?

223
00:16:16.709 --> 00:16:19.372
Wouldn't want to prescribe a lozenge
if there's any doubt about
its efficacy, huh?

224
00:16:19.446 --> 00:16:23.611
You once asked me
why I think I'm always right,
and I realized that you're right.

225
00:16:23.686 --> 00:16:26.815
At least, I think you're right.
I don't really know, now do I?

226
00:16:28.059 --> 00:16:32.394
- Hey. I'm here.
- Go home. Drink some hot tea.

227
00:16:37.239 --> 00:16:39.435
[Exhales]
Excellent counsel.

228
00:16:39.509 --> 00:16:42.843
Negative on parvovirus B-19.

229
00:16:42.914 --> 00:16:46.078
I'm impressed.
Thank you.
I was born to run gels.

230
00:16:46.152 --> 00:16:49.281
I meant about Chase.
What about Chase?

231
00:16:50.458 --> 00:16:53.019
Well, the man has no
physical interest in you.

232
00:16:53.096 --> 00:16:58.593
He has a completely professional
relationship with you, respects you
as a colleague and a doctor.

233
00:16:58.670 --> 00:17:02.664
And yet, he can't look at you
without thinking sex.

234
00:17:02.743 --> 00:17:04.677
Because I asked
what kind of sex could kill you?

235
00:17:04.746 --> 00:17:08.376
You now have total control
over your relationship with him.

236
00:17:08.452 --> 00:17:12.787
So, a woman can't express
her interest in sex without it
being some professional power play?

237
00:17:12.858 --> 00:17:16.693
No. If you look the way you do
and you say what you said,

238
00:17:16.763 --> 00:17:19.665
you have to be aware of the effect
that it's going to have on men.

239
00:17:19.735 --> 00:17:23.069
- Men should grow up.
- Yeah, and dogs should stop
licking themselves.

240
00:17:23.139 --> 00:17:24.731
It's not gonna happen.
What's going on?

241
00:17:26.211 --> 00:17:28.737
- Yeah, what are you doing here?
- Looking for you guys.

242
00:17:28.814 --> 00:17:30.907
- Why didn't you page us?
- 'Cause I knew you'd be here.

243
00:17:30.984 --> 00:17:33.077
Who told him?
No one.

244
00:17:33.154 --> 00:17:37.752
I assume you're trying to prove
my crazy, two-illness theory wrong,
so, obviously, you're gonna be in the lab.

245
00:17:37.827 --> 00:17:39.852
- You spin the urine?
- Not yet.

246
00:17:39.930 --> 00:17:42.456
Talk to me when you have.

247
00:17:49.611 --> 00:17:54.107
What'd you find out?
Kidney failure.
It's acute interstitial nephritis.

248
00:17:55.186 --> 00:18:00.421
- I wonder if that's significant.
- It means the antibiotics
didn't cause the kidney failure.

249
00:18:00.493 --> 00:18:02.427
How'd you know?

250
00:18:02.496 --> 00:18:05.955
If you guys hadn't been so busy
trying to prove me wrong,
you might've checked in on the poor kid.

251
00:18:06.035 --> 00:18:08.334
You visited a patient?

252
00:18:08.405 --> 00:18:12.467
I was sitting by his bed all morning, just
so he'd know someone was there for him.

253
00:18:12.545 --> 00:18:14.342
I looked in on him.
He's much better.

254
00:18:14.414 --> 00:18:17.350
Ergo, the treatment's working.
Ergo, me right, you wrong.

255
00:18:17.418 --> 00:18:19.785
Hey, I'm glad for the kid.

256
00:18:23.427 --> 00:18:26.761
That smugness of yours
really is an attractive quality.
Thank you.

257
00:18:26.832 --> 00:18:31.167
It was either that
or get my hair highlighted.
Smugness is easier to maintain.

258
00:18:31.238 --> 00:18:34.231
I get that you're not
a big believer in the
"catching flies with honey" approach,

259
00:18:34.310 --> 00:18:37.803
but do you honestly think
you'll collect a jarful
by cleverly taunting them?

260
00:18:37.881 --> 00:18:40.715
Flies, no. Doctors, sure.
If I'd said to Foreman,

261
00:18:40.786 --> 00:18:44.314
"Nice try. Great guess,
but sorry, not this time,"
what do you think he'd be doing right now?

262
00:18:44.390 --> 00:18:48.725
I think he'd go home
not feeling like a piece of crap.
Exactly.

263
00:18:48.797 --> 00:18:52.461
You want him to
feel like a piece of crap?
No. I don't want him going home.

264
00:18:56.142 --> 00:18:59.306
Dr. Foreman.
[Coughs]

265
00:18:59.379 --> 00:19:02.713
Still have the cough.
I'm feeling a lot better though.

266
00:19:02.785 --> 00:19:05.949
His fever is gone.
His rash is going away. [Chuckles]

267
00:19:06.022 --> 00:19:10.016
I see.
Is everything okay?

268
00:19:10.095 --> 00:19:13.930
Just ordering some tests.
Absolutely nothing to worry about.

269
00:19:27.120 --> 00:19:30.056
[Game Beeping]

270
00:19:30.124 --> 00:19:35.928
- How much longer?
- 9:30. I figure she was on
the eighth hole when I paged her.

271
00:19:40.105 --> 00:19:42.438
You probably got another half hour.

272
00:19:47.349 --> 00:19:53.256
I ran a T.S.H., T3 and T4.
The patient's negative for hypothyroidism.
I'm not talking about you.

273
00:19:53.325 --> 00:19:57.353
The fact that he's getting better would
indicate the unreliability of the tests.

274
00:19:57.431 --> 00:20:00.424
If I'm right and it's a viral infection,
one of two things always happen:

275
00:20:00.501 --> 00:20:03.994
The patient dies,
or the patient's immune system
fights off the invader.

276
00:20:04.074 --> 00:20:05.974
What's with her?

277
00:20:06.043 --> 00:20:10.037
Her leg hurts after running six miles.
Who knows? Could be anything.

278
00:20:10.116 --> 00:20:13.177
He's getting better.
That doesn't prove you're right.
That just proves he's getting better.

279
00:20:14.589 --> 00:20:18.151
It-It's not two illnesses.
It can't be two illnesses.

280
00:20:18.227 --> 00:20:21.095
I am so glad you work here.

281
00:20:21.165 --> 00:20:24.829
[Exhales] If I'm right,
the antibiotics you prescribed...

282
00:20:24.904 --> 00:20:28.068
could box his kidneys and liver,
impeding his ability
to fight off the virus.

283
00:20:28.142 --> 00:20:33.309
- It could kill him.
- Well, that certainly would be a concern.

284
00:20:33.383 --> 00:20:35.112
Fifty bucks?

285
00:20:35.185 --> 00:20:37.882
Don't look away.
The space monkeys
will be all over you.

286
00:20:37.956 --> 00:20:40.551
- You wanna bet on the patient's health?
- You think that's bad luck?

287
00:20:40.627 --> 00:20:45.259
You think that God will smite him
because of our insensitivity?

288
00:20:45.334 --> 00:20:47.735
Well, if God does,
you make a quick 50.

289
00:20:47.804 --> 00:20:50.399
- [Scoffs]
- [Beeps]

290
00:20:50.474 --> 00:20:54.468
- Oh.
- Go check his white blood count.

291
00:20:54.547 --> 00:20:57.711
If he's fighting off a virus
like you think, it'll be way up.

292
00:21:03.560 --> 00:21:07.759
Hey. Cuddy said you needed a consult.
What's up? I'm busy.

293
00:21:16.612 --> 00:21:18.705
Oh!

294
00:21:24.391 --> 00:21:27.384
- I was just being glib.
- You haven't said anything.

295
00:21:27.462 --> 00:21:33.266
No. Before, when I was talking about
Brandon's girlfriend thinking sex
could kill you.

296
00:21:33.337 --> 00:21:35.636
I was just making a joke
because I was uncomfortable.

297
00:21:35.707 --> 00:21:38.575
Oh, I don't even
remember what you said.
I'm uncomfortable about sex.

298
00:21:40.447 --> 00:21:45.079
- Well, we don't have to talk about this.
- Sex could kill you.

299
00:21:45.154 --> 00:21:48.249
Do you know what
the human body goes through
when you have sex?

300
00:21:48.325 --> 00:21:50.817
Pupils dilate. Arteries constrict.

301
00:21:50.896 --> 00:21:53.923
Core temperature rises, heart races,
blood pressure skyrockets.

302
00:21:54.000 --> 00:21:57.300
Respiration becomes rapid and shallow.

303
00:21:57.372 --> 00:22:00.706
The brain fires bursts of
electrical impulses
from nowhere to nowhere.

304
00:22:00.777 --> 00:22:02.574
Secretions spit out of every gland,

305
00:22:02.646 --> 00:22:06.811
and the muscles tense
and spasm like you're lifting
three times your body weight.

306
00:22:06.886 --> 00:22:11.552
It's violent, it's ugly,
and it's messy.

307
00:22:11.626 --> 00:22:17.464
And if God hadn't made it
unbelievably fun, the human race
would've died out eons ago.

308
00:22:20.539 --> 00:22:23.031
Men are lucky
they can only have one orgasm.

309
00:22:23.109 --> 00:22:27.137
You know that women
can have an hour-long orgasm?

310
00:22:27.215 --> 00:22:29.206
Hey, Foreman. What's up?

311
00:22:29.285 --> 00:22:31.516
- Hey, Foreman.
- Hey.

312
00:22:32.523 --> 00:22:37.758
- White cell count isn't up, is it?
- No. We were both wrong.

313
00:22:37.831 --> 00:22:40.995
White cell count is down-
way down-and dropping.

314
00:22:41.069 --> 00:22:44.562
His immune system is shot.
We need to get him into a clean room.

315
00:22:50.583 --> 00:22:53.576
[Chase]
Can you walk, Brandon?

316
00:22:53.653 --> 00:22:55.644
Yeah. A little.

317
00:22:55.723 --> 00:23:00.185
Okay. 'Cause we'll need to
leave the chair outside. Thank you.

318
00:23:00.263 --> 00:23:02.892
Where's April? April?

319
00:23:02.968 --> 00:23:07.805
Can you take that chair, please?
Thank you.
Yes, Robert.

320
00:23:07.875 --> 00:23:11.209
I'll need to take your, um-
your mask and your robe too.

321
00:23:18.089 --> 00:23:22.687
You might wanna block your ears
for this, it's quite loud.

322
00:23:26.134 --> 00:23:29.263
[Loud Hissing]

323
00:23:33.278 --> 00:23:35.439
Something's made him
immuno-compromised.

324
00:23:35.514 --> 00:23:40.010
His white blood cell count is down,
which means his body
can't fight off infections.

325
00:23:40.088 --> 00:23:44.423
If he gets sick, he'll die.
Sick? How sick?

326
00:23:44.495 --> 00:23:47.158
Lfhe gets a cold, he'll die.

327
00:23:54.976 --> 00:23:57.377
[Coughing]

328
00:23:57.446 --> 00:24:03.284
Okay. I'm gonna push the needle
into your hip bone
and take some of the marrow.

329
00:24:05.792 --> 00:24:07.726
That's not so bad.

330
00:24:07.795 --> 00:24:12.234
Uh-uh. That was just the anesthetic.
[Instrument Clatters On Table]

331
00:24:12.301 --> 00:24:16.967
The core biopsy needle,
it's a bit bigger.

332
00:24:17.041 --> 00:24:22.208
Hey, man. Take a deep breath.
This-This is gonna hurt... a lot.

333
00:24:25.053 --> 00:24:27.682
[Gasping]

334
00:24:27.757 --> 00:24:31.091
Your marrow makes the blood cells.

335
00:24:32.932 --> 00:24:35.299
We take a peek at it
under a microscope,

336
00:24:35.369 --> 00:24:39.363
and maybe we find a viral infection.

337
00:24:39.441 --> 00:24:41.466
Maybe we find some fibrosis.

338
00:24:41.544 --> 00:24:45.538
Something to explain why
your blood count is so low.

339
00:24:46.551 --> 00:24:48.485
There we go.

340
00:24:49.989 --> 00:24:52.220
One step closer to an answer.

341
00:24:52.294 --> 00:24:55.287
[Shaky Breath]
If you don't find one,

342
00:24:57.167 --> 00:24:59.728
I can't stay here forever.

343
00:25:01.540 --> 00:25:06.570
[Panting]

344
00:25:08.083 --> 00:25:11.110
- [House] The patient could've died.
- The one with the pulled muscle?

345
00:25:11.187 --> 00:25:16.024
Those symptoms are consistent
with a dozen other conditions.

346
00:25:16.094 --> 00:25:18.996
- [Stammers]
I'm entitled to a consult.
- You are not getting out of clinic duty.

347
00:25:19.066 --> 00:25:23.698
Come on. You got a hundred other
idiot doctors in this building who go...

348
00:25:23.772 --> 00:25:27.470
all warm and fuzzy every time
they pull a toy car out of a nose-
you don't need me here.

349
00:25:27.545 --> 00:25:30.709
No, I don't. But working with people
actually makes you a better doctor.

350
00:25:30.782 --> 00:25:33.877
When did I sign up for that course?
When did I give you
the impression that I care?

351
00:25:35.222 --> 00:25:38.886
Working in this clinic obviously instills
a deep sense of compassion.

352
00:25:38.961 --> 00:25:43.457
I've got your home number, right?
In case anything comes up at 3:00
in the morning.

353
00:25:43.534 --> 00:25:46.163
It's not gonna work.
You know why?

354
00:25:46.238 --> 00:25:48.730
Because this is fun.

355
00:25:48.808 --> 00:25:52.711
You think of something to make
me miserable. I think of something
to make you miserable-

356
00:25:52.781 --> 00:25:57.447
It's a game, and I'm gonna win
because I got a head start.
You are already miserable.

357
00:26:01.427 --> 00:26:03.327
Uh-
Is this important?

358
00:26:03.397 --> 00:26:05.331
Uh, no.
Good.

359
00:26:07.336 --> 00:26:09.270
What's with you and her?
Don't.

360
00:26:09.339 --> 00:26:11.500
You have a thing for her?
The only people who can get to you-

361
00:26:11.575 --> 00:26:13.736
No. There is not a thin line
between love and hate.

362
00:26:13.812 --> 00:26:18.979
There is, in fact, a Great Wall of China,
with armed sentries posted every 20 feet
between love and hate.

363
00:26:19.052 --> 00:26:21.385
Thirty-six Vicodin.
Who's the patient?

364
00:26:21.456 --> 00:26:23.287
I am.
You can't-

365
00:26:23.359 --> 00:26:25.851
Dr. Wilson is
the prescribing physician.
Yeah.

366
00:26:25.929 --> 00:26:30.094
You will lie, cheat and steal
to get what you want, but you're
incapable of kissing a little ass?

367
00:26:30.169 --> 00:26:32.103
[Pills Rattle]
We all have our limitations.

368
00:26:32.172 --> 00:26:36.405
House?
Wrong bottle. Do me a favor.

369
00:26:36.478 --> 00:26:41.474
Take one of these,
wait five minutes for it to kick in,
then find Cuddy and kiss her ass.

370
00:26:43.154 --> 00:26:46.147
What was the kid's first symptom?

371
00:26:46.226 --> 00:26:49.719
You did the history.
Of his 800 symptoms,
which one hit him first?

372
00:26:49.797 --> 00:26:51.731
Uh, the cough.

373
00:27:49.317 --> 00:27:53.652
[Coughing]

374
00:28:05.341 --> 00:28:08.334
[Erratic Breathing]

375
00:28:18.527 --> 00:28:20.461
Gout.

376
00:28:26.304 --> 00:28:28.933
Um, are we talking about Brandon?
Gout?

377
00:28:29.009 --> 00:28:30.943
Uric acid crystals in the joints?

378
00:28:31.011 --> 00:28:36.883
The symptoms are pain,
swelling, redness, stiffness.
Not one of which do I see on that board.

379
00:28:36.953 --> 00:28:39.252
Because he doesn't have gout.
[Makes Popping Sound]

380
00:28:41.593 --> 00:28:43.926
Every day, cells die.

381
00:28:46.935 --> 00:28:50.394
We survive because the remaining cells
divide and replace the losses.

382
00:28:51.908 --> 00:28:57.576
The colchicine, a gout medicine,
blocks mitosis and stops cell division,

383
00:28:58.752 --> 00:29:02.154
which will result in
abdominal pain, rash,

384
00:29:02.224 --> 00:29:06.890
nausea, fever, kidney failure,
low blood pressure...

385
00:29:06.964 --> 00:29:08.989
and will also mess with the bone marrow.

386
00:29:09.067 --> 00:29:11.228
But he doesn't have gout.
Why would he have gout medication?

387
00:29:11.303 --> 00:29:14.762
Because you guys were right.
He didn't have two conditions
at the exact same time.

388
00:29:14.842 --> 00:29:18.301
First, he got a cough.
And because he's an idiot,
he went to a doctor.

389
00:29:18.380 --> 00:29:22.340
In order to justify charging $200,
that doctor felt
he should actually do something.

390
00:29:22.420 --> 00:29:25.083
Oops. He wrote a prescription.

391
00:29:25.157 --> 00:29:28.992
Seven thousand people die each year
from pharmacy screwups.

392
00:29:29.063 --> 00:29:30.997
Not nearly as many as die
from doctor screwups,

393
00:29:31.066 --> 00:29:33.695
but still, not something
they use in their promotional materials.

394
00:29:33.769 --> 00:29:37.262
The pharmacist gave him
gout medicine instead of cough medicine.

395
00:29:37.341 --> 00:29:39.502
And the only thing it wouldn't do,

396
00:29:39.578 --> 00:29:43.572
it would do absolutely nothing
to relieve his cough.

397
00:29:43.651 --> 00:29:45.676
Occam's Razor-

398
00:29:45.754 --> 00:29:49.555
the simplest explanation is
almost always that somebody screwed up.

399
00:29:49.625 --> 00:29:53.619
But once he checked into this hospital,
he was completely in our control.

400
00:29:53.698 --> 00:29:55.859
Our food, our pills, our everything.

401
00:29:55.935 --> 00:29:58.598
So even if you're right,
no more gout medication.

402
00:29:58.673 --> 00:30:01.666
He'd either continue to deteriorate,
or he would've gotten better.

403
00:30:01.744 --> 00:30:04.578
But he got better,
and then he got worse.

404
00:30:04.647 --> 00:30:07.116
It doesn't fit.
It doesn't make sense.

405
00:30:07.184 --> 00:30:10.177
Okay. Two people screwed up.

406
00:30:10.256 --> 00:30:12.782
Not as simple as one, but-

407
00:30:22.306 --> 00:30:24.969
He's resting. He's-
I'm Dr. House.

408
00:30:25.044 --> 00:30:29.038
I'm your son's physician.
Oh. You're the one
we haven't met yet.

409
00:30:29.116 --> 00:30:33.521
You're the one he hasn't met.
How can you treat someone
without meeting them?

410
00:30:33.589 --> 00:30:36.753
It's easy if you don't
give a crap about him.

411
00:30:36.828 --> 00:30:39.320
That's a good thing.

412
00:30:39.398 --> 00:30:43.803
If emotions made you act rationally, well,
they wouldn't be called emotions, right?

413
00:30:43.871 --> 00:30:47.706
That's why we have
this nice division of labor.
You hold his hand, I get him better.

414
00:30:47.777 --> 00:30:50.440
If I start tucking him in at night,
well, that's not fair to you guys.

415
00:30:50.514 --> 00:30:52.949
And if you start prescribing medicine,
well, that's not fair to me.

416
00:30:53.018 --> 00:30:56.750
So, what I wanna know is,
who stepped on my side of the net?

417
00:30:56.824 --> 00:31:01.695
Who cared enough
to get stupid enough
to give him his cough medicine?

418
00:31:01.764 --> 00:31:03.698
When we checked in, Dr. Foreman-

419
00:31:03.767 --> 00:31:07.761
Tuesday, he's getting better.
Wednesday, he's getting sick again.

420
00:31:07.840 --> 00:31:11.538
Somebody gave him
his cough medicine Wednesday.

421
00:31:15.451 --> 00:31:18.444
Come on. Nobody's gonna be mad.

422
00:31:18.522 --> 00:31:22.015
I just wanna know
who tried to kill the kid.

423
00:31:26.534 --> 00:31:30.494
- Dr. House, maybe we should-
- His throat was sore.

424
00:31:33.510 --> 00:31:36.844
Page Dr. Occam.
He's gonna wanna hear about this.
I'm sorry.

425
00:31:36.915 --> 00:31:41.080
He was coughing,
and I just wanted to help him-
Aren't you a dear.

426
00:31:41.154 --> 00:31:45.023
Where are the pills?
He took the last of'em before
he was switched into that room.

427
00:31:45.094 --> 00:31:46.755
They're all gone?
It was just cough medicine.

428
00:31:46.830 --> 00:31:49.459
No, it wasn't.
Where's the bottle?

429
00:31:57.812 --> 00:32:00.509
We need to know
exactly what you put in this bottle.

430
00:32:00.583 --> 00:32:02.517
We think it was colchicine,
a gout medication.

431
00:32:02.586 --> 00:32:05.579
If the prescription said cough medicine,
that's what I dispensed.

432
00:32:05.658 --> 00:32:07.819
The family is prepared
to waive liability, all right?

433
00:32:07.894 --> 00:32:12.059
We just need to know what it was,
what dosage it was-
It was cough medicine.

434
00:32:12.134 --> 00:32:14.626
Refill it.

435
00:32:16.573 --> 00:32:20.408
He's gonna be okay.
You don't know that.

436
00:32:22.315 --> 00:32:25.808
Does Brandon like
that quality in you?

437
00:32:25.887 --> 00:32:28.048
You're a little negative.

438
00:32:29.893 --> 00:32:34.263
Things don't always
work out for the best.
Doesn't hurt to hope they do.

439
00:32:34.333 --> 00:32:39.170
No. Not unless that makes you figure
you can do whatever you want,
like give people cough medicine.

440
00:32:40.608 --> 00:32:45.070
This is cough medication.
This is what Brandon
was supposed to get.

441
00:32:45.148 --> 00:32:47.845
They're small, round and yellow.

442
00:32:47.919 --> 00:32:52.254
Can you tell this man what
the pills in your son's medicine bottle
actually looked like?

443
00:32:54.595 --> 00:32:57.190
They were small, round and yellow,
exactly like this.

444
00:32:57.265 --> 00:32:59.426
Those were the pills
that Brandon was taking.

445
00:32:59.502 --> 00:33:04.601
Hey, I'm just a pharmacist,
but I know what
cough medicine looks like, Doctor.

446
00:33:08.782 --> 00:33:12.116
[House]
It was so perfect.
It was beautiful.

447
00:33:12.187 --> 00:33:15.351
Beauty often seduces us
on the road to truth.

448
00:33:17.028 --> 00:33:19.862
And triteness kicks us in the nads.

449
00:33:19.932 --> 00:33:23.096
So true.
This doesn't bother you?

450
00:33:23.170 --> 00:33:26.504
That you were wrong?
I try to work through the pain.

451
00:33:26.575 --> 00:33:31.571
I was not wrong.
Everything I said was true.
It fit. It was elegant.

452
00:33:31.649 --> 00:33:37.317
- So, reality was wrong?
- [Sighs] Reality's almost always wrong.

453
00:33:43.332 --> 00:33:46.496
The cough medicine did something.

454
00:33:46.571 --> 00:33:49.268
[Exhales]
Aggravated the condition.

455
00:33:50.409 --> 00:33:52.400
It's all over the place.
Must be in his blood.

456
00:33:52.479 --> 00:33:55.210
- What if it is his blood?
- Lymphoma?

457
00:33:55.284 --> 00:33:57.617
Unless you've got something better.

458
00:33:57.687 --> 00:34:01.180
We foolishly ruled out lymphoma because
his C.T. Scan showed no adenopathy,

459
00:34:01.258 --> 00:34:05.959
C.B.C. Showed a normal differen-smear,
bone marrow showed no-
Screw the tests.

460
00:34:06.033 --> 00:34:08.935
Do an exploratory laparotomy
and find out what's in there.

461
00:34:09.003 --> 00:34:13.704
He has no blood pressure,
no immune system and no kidneys.
Surgery will kill him.

462
00:34:13.777 --> 00:34:17.805
Yeah, you're right.
Let's stick with the wrong pill theory.

463
00:34:21.822 --> 00:34:25.156
I'll schedule him for surgery.

464
00:34:29.166 --> 00:34:32.330
[Foreman]
Okay, Brandon, we're running this tube
through your heart...

465
00:34:32.404 --> 00:34:35.499
and into the pulmonary arteries
in your lungs.

466
00:34:35.575 --> 00:34:39.012
[Cameron] The sensors will give us
information we need for the exploratory
surgery later this afternoon.

467
00:34:43.554 --> 00:34:46.388
- My fingers are numb.
- Try not to move.

468
00:34:46.458 --> 00:34:51.727
We're in the right atrium,
trying to catch the flow
through the tricuspid valve.

469
00:34:51.798 --> 00:34:54.495
[Chase]
I think the catheter's curling
in the atrium.

470
00:34:54.570 --> 00:34:59.032
Got it. We're in the R.V. Now.

471
00:34:59.110 --> 00:35:01.739
[Beeps]
Ectopy.

472
00:35:01.813 --> 00:35:05.215
- You must've irritated the heart wall.
- It'll calm down.

473
00:35:05.286 --> 00:35:08.120
- He can't tolerate any cardiac arrhythmia.
Pull back.
- He needs the surgery.

474
00:35:12.596 --> 00:35:16.431
[Monitor Beeping Rapidly]

475
00:35:18.838 --> 00:35:23.334
- [High-pitched Tone]
- Pressure's dropped.

476
00:35:23.412 --> 00:35:25.973
- You still with us, Brandon?
- Get the curtains.

477
00:35:26.049 --> 00:35:28.644
V.F.

478
00:35:30.488 --> 00:35:33.652
[Sustained Beep]

479
00:35:33.727 --> 00:35:36.959
[Crying]

480
00:35:37.031 --> 00:35:41.332
[Chase]
Charging. Clear.

481
00:35:44.175 --> 00:35:47.839
- [Rhythmic Beeping]
- [Exhales] Sinus rhythm.

482
00:35:49.383 --> 00:35:51.579
I got a pulse.

483
00:35:51.653 --> 00:35:53.952
[Sighs]

484
00:35:54.023 --> 00:35:56.822
Yeah, but no surgery today.

485
00:36:03.503 --> 00:36:07.031
- How're you doing?
- Okay.

486
00:36:07.109 --> 00:36:09.442
Great. I'm doing good too.

487
00:36:09.512 --> 00:36:12.846
I get to knock off an hour early today.
You know why?

488
00:36:12.917 --> 00:36:16.684
Because I kissed my boss's ass.
Do you ever do that?

489
00:36:16.756 --> 00:36:19.419
I think she just said yes 'cause
she wants to reinforce that behavior.

490
00:36:19.494 --> 00:36:23.158
Wants me to kiss a lot of
other people's ass,
like she wants me to kiss yours.

491
00:36:23.232 --> 00:36:27.397
What would you want?
A doctor who holds your hand
while you die,

492
00:36:27.471 --> 00:36:29.906
or a doctor who ignores you
while you get better?

493
00:36:29.975 --> 00:36:33.912
I guess it would particularly suck
to have a doctor
who ignores you while you die.

494
00:36:35.250 --> 00:36:37.913
- I should go.
- You think it's gonna come out on its own?

495
00:36:42.927 --> 00:36:46.659
Are we talking
bigger than a breadbasket?

496
00:36:46.733 --> 00:36:49.601
Because, actually,
it will come out on its own.

497
00:36:49.670 --> 00:36:54.666
Which for small stuff is no problem.
It's wrapped up in a nice,
soft package, and plop.

498
00:36:54.745 --> 00:36:56.576
Big stuff, you're gonna rip something,

499
00:36:56.648 --> 00:36:59.345
which, speaking medically,
is when the fun stops.
How did you-

500
00:36:59.418 --> 00:37:03.446
You've been here half an hour,
you haven't sat down.
That tells me its location.

501
00:37:03.524 --> 00:37:06.688
You haven't told me what it is.
That tells me it's humiliating.

502
00:37:06.762 --> 00:37:10.631
You have a little birdie carved on
your arm. That tells me you have
a high tolerance for humiliation.

503
00:37:10.701 --> 00:37:14.069
So I figure it's not hemorrhoids.

504
00:37:17.378 --> 00:37:19.711
I've been a doctor 20 years.
You're not gonna surprise me.

505
00:37:21.650 --> 00:37:24.984
[Exhales]
It's an MP3 player.

506
00:37:30.930 --> 00:37:33.091
Mm.

507
00:37:33.167 --> 00:37:39.005
Is it- Is it because of the size,
or the shape,

508
00:37:39.076 --> 00:37:41.807
or is it the pounding bass line?

509
00:37:41.880 --> 00:37:44.577
What are we gonna do?

510
00:37:47.822 --> 00:37:50.257
- I'm gonna wait.
- For what?

511
00:37:52.429 --> 00:37:54.590
Okay. It's 3:00. I'm off.

512
00:37:54.665 --> 00:37:57.999
Would you tell Dr. Cuddy
there's a patient in Exam Room Two
needs her attention?

513
00:37:58.070 --> 00:38:01.234
And the R.I.A.A. Wants her to check
for illegal downloads.

514
00:38:02.510 --> 00:38:05.002
Brandon's not ready for surgery.
Okay.

515
00:38:05.080 --> 00:38:09.245
Let's leave it a couple of weeks.
He should be feeling better by then.
Oh, wait. Which way does time go?

516
00:38:09.320 --> 00:38:12.654
He crashed during prep.
He's also experiencing
pain in his fingers.

517
00:38:12.724 --> 00:38:14.715
Think some bug
may have gotten in the clean room.

518
00:38:14.794 --> 00:38:19.290
I think we should double his dosage
of G-CSF to temporarily boost
his white blood cell count.

519
00:38:19.367 --> 00:38:23.304
Pain in his fingers. Right.

520
00:38:31.419 --> 00:38:33.888
Hi again.
He can't-

521
00:38:33.956 --> 00:38:36.949
Where's he going?
[Hissing]

522
00:38:38.062 --> 00:38:40.223
Hey. How you all doing?

523
00:38:40.298 --> 00:38:44.760
Interesting fact. Every seven years,
it's a whole new you.
Inspiring metaphor, huh?

524
00:38:44.838 --> 00:38:48.502
Dr. House,
this is a clean room.
Yeah. I read the sign.

525
00:38:48.577 --> 00:38:53.278
But cells of different organs
reproduce at different rates.

526
00:38:53.351 --> 00:38:56.844
- [Groans]
- So, you get a new kidney
every three years.

527
00:38:56.922 --> 00:38:59.255
Get a new stomach lining every week.

528
00:38:59.326 --> 00:39:03.559
This is why colchicine poisoning
causes all these symptoms,
but not all at once.

529
00:39:03.633 --> 00:39:06.125
But we went to the pharmacy.
We saw the pills.

530
00:39:06.203 --> 00:39:09.196
Colchicine does its damage
in a very specific order.

531
00:39:09.274 --> 00:39:13.541
First of all, there's the pain in
the abdomen, the rash, the fever.
Isn't that what you got first?

532
00:39:13.613 --> 00:39:18.075
Then the kidneys go,
which is exactly what happened to-

533
00:39:18.153 --> 00:39:20.053
- Brandon.
- Right.

534
00:39:20.123 --> 00:39:25.153
Then it screws up your bone marrow,
and then neuropathy.

535
00:39:25.230 --> 00:39:28.758
[Brandon Groans]
A painful tingling
in the fingers and toes.

536
00:39:28.835 --> 00:39:31.396
And what do you suppose
happens after that?
[Grunts]

537
00:39:35.412 --> 00:39:39.247
Hair loss. The bad news is...

538
00:39:39.318 --> 00:39:42.755
your special boy is doing drugs.
[Mom]
No, he's not.

539
00:39:42.822 --> 00:39:45.291
Ecstasy?
No.

540
00:39:45.360 --> 00:39:50.356
- Twice with Dan and Mike.
- You know what they cut that stuff with?

541
00:39:50.434 --> 00:39:54.930
Apparently, colchicine.
Unless you ingested the colchicine
through your contact lens solution,

542
00:39:55.007 --> 00:39:57.704
or skin cream
or some other drug you're lying about.

543
00:39:57.777 --> 00:40:02.648
I don't know how it happened.
I don't care how it happened.
It happened. Start, uh-

544
00:40:02.719 --> 00:40:06.212
- Brandon.
- Lovely name.

545
00:40:06.290 --> 00:40:10.455
Start Brandon on FAB fragments,
and get him some Tylenol
for the hair I pulled out.

546
00:40:10.529 --> 00:40:12.690
And get some air in here.

547
00:40:14.469 --> 00:40:17.132
Make a note.
I should never doubt myself.

548
00:40:17.206 --> 00:40:20.870
I think you'll remember.
You know, it wouldn't hurt you
to be wrong every now and then.

549
00:40:20.945 --> 00:40:23.312
What, you don't care about
these people?

550
00:40:23.382 --> 00:40:27.376
[Monitor Beeping]

551
00:40:27.454 --> 00:40:31.789
The colchicine interferes with
the ability of the heart muscle
to contract,

552
00:40:31.861 --> 00:40:34.695
pumping blood,
lowering your blood pressure.

553
00:40:37.035 --> 00:40:41.531
The antibodies we're giving you
should neutralize the colchicine,

554
00:40:43.210 --> 00:40:46.009
allowing your heart
to beat at its normal rate.

555
00:40:47.016 --> 00:40:50.350
When will you know?

556
00:40:50.421 --> 00:40:52.355
We know now.

557
00:40:53.693 --> 00:40:56.356
Thank God.
[Laughs]

558
00:40:56.430 --> 00:40:58.364
Mmm.

559
00:41:02.539 --> 00:41:06.032
[Exhales, Laughs]

560
00:41:18.462 --> 00:41:22.399
Big weekend?
It's not for me.
I'm fully stocked.

561
00:41:22.468 --> 00:41:26.930
- Cuddy got you doing inventory?
- Nope. Trying to solve that kid's case.

562
00:41:27.007 --> 00:41:29.670
The gout medicine O.D.?
Yeah.

563
00:41:29.745 --> 00:41:33.147
The fact that I know it's a gout
medicine O.D. Would indicate
the case is already solved.

564
00:41:33.217 --> 00:41:35.151
Well, you'd be wrong.

565
00:41:35.220 --> 00:41:40.057
What about the fact that
the kid is now- I believe
the technical term is- "not sick"?

566
00:41:40.127 --> 00:41:42.460
You know how many forms
of colchicine there are on the market?

567
00:41:42.530 --> 00:41:44.999
- Stop it.
- Neither do I. But it's a lot.

568
00:41:45.067 --> 00:41:48.265
Pills, powders, liquids, I. V. Fluids.

569
00:41:48.339 --> 00:41:52.504
Somewhere at a party, in his coffee,
up his nose, in his ear, this kid had some.

570
00:41:52.578 --> 00:41:54.478
You're not happy with
your Ecstasy theory?

571
00:41:54.548 --> 00:41:56.881
- He said he used it twice.
- People lie.

572
00:41:56.951 --> 00:41:59.147
- If you're gonna lie, it's-
- You know what? I'm not interested.

573
00:41:59.221 --> 00:42:03.488
- Not curious?
- No. Because I'm well-adjusted.

574
00:42:03.561 --> 00:42:06.360
Right.

575
00:42:08.368 --> 00:42:11.668
Temperature's normal.
I want cousin Sharon there.

576
00:42:11.740 --> 00:42:13.971
If we invite Sharon,
we have to invite all the cousins.

577
00:42:14.043 --> 00:42:17.241
So what? My side of the family
doesn't need anything.

578
00:42:17.314 --> 00:42:21.649
[All Chuckle]
[Coughing]

579
00:42:21.720 --> 00:42:25.213
I don't suppose I could have
some of those cough pills, huh?
They're okay, right?

580
00:42:25.293 --> 00:42:27.762
- Yes. You're doing great.
- You should invite Dr. House.

581
00:42:27.830 --> 00:42:30.698
- [Brandon] Will he come?
- No. But he'll send a gift.

582
00:42:30.767 --> 00:42:33.259
[Laughs]
I'll make sure it's a good one.

583
00:42:33.337 --> 00:42:37.001
There's a letter
on the back of these pills.

584
00:42:38.078 --> 00:42:40.343
Your old pills
didn't have a letter on them?

585
00:42:40.415 --> 00:42:43.715
No. Round and yellow,
but no letter.

586
00:42:50.729 --> 00:42:53.961
Well, these will help your cough.

587
00:42:57.640 --> 00:42:59.801
Hey, you wanna go get some-
No.

588
00:44:03.769 --> 00:44:05.031
That's some bad hat, Harry.

9999
00:00:0.500 --> 00:00:2.00
<font color="#ffff00" size=14>www.tvsubtitles.net</font>

